From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] server: log PS4 protocol failures to klog

The server PRX's stderr is not captured on the console. When a client request
has a protocol error, emit the same bounded reason to klog before the server
terminates the client thread. This carries forward the established PS4
diagnostic from src/wine-patches-ps4/0865; this patch has a new queue number
because upstream already uses 0865 for a different patch.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -145,6 +145,24 @@ void fatal_protocol_error( struct thread *thread, const char *err, ... )
     fprintf( stderr, "Protocol error:%04x: ", thread->id );
     vfprintf( stderr, err, args );
     va_end( args );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* This PRX's stderr is not captured on the console. Preserve the protocol
+     * failure reason in klog before kill_thread tears down its request path. */
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        char line[256];
+        int n;
+
+        n = snprintf( line, sizeof(line), "wineserver: protocol error %04x: ", thread->id );
+        if (n > 0 && n < (int)sizeof(line))
+        {
+            va_start( args, err );
+            vsnprintf( line + n, sizeof(line) - n, err, args );
+            va_end( args );
+            sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     thread->exit_code = 1;
     kill_thread( thread, 1 );
 }
